#!/usr/bin/python3
"""hearth-vnc: Settings › Remote desktop (SetRemoteDesktop.qml). This PC's desktop in any VNC app (TigerVNC, Remmina,
KRDC, RealVNC-compatible viewers that do VeNCrypt), on your other devices through Tailscale, or your home network too.
Never the internet. Off by default; nothing about it is on in the image.

The screen comes from the desktop's screen-sharing portal (hearth_screencast: KWin's, or labwc's wlr backend), the
keyboard and mouse through the portal's RemoteDesktop on KWin; on labwc (whose portal has no RemoteDesktop) through a
virtual keyboard and mouse (uinput, which Hearth lets the person at the PC use), else it's view-only and says so.
The portal asks at the PC the first time; KWin remembers that answer (its restore token, kept in the state folder).

Security: VeNCrypt only. Every connection is TLS: X509Plain (this PC's own certificate, made here, its SHA-256
fingerprint shown in Settings to compare with what the viewer shows) for everyone, and TLSPlain (anonymous TLS) only
for Tailscale addresses, whose WireGuard tunnel already proves who they are. The password is in your keyring
(libsecret, secret-tool), never in a file, never logged or shown. Connections from anywhere but Tailscale (and your home
network when you chose it) are refused before anything is sent; 5 wrong passwords lock that address out for 5 minutes.
Every connection is a notification and the bar's capture dot (CaptureIndicator.qml) until it ends.

Files:
  ~/.config/nimbus/remote-vnc.json     your choices: on, reach (tailscale|home), viewOnly. Written only when you change
                                       one, through hearth_settings_io (atomic, .bak, merged; defaults never saved)
  ~/.local/share/nimbus/vnc/           this PC's certificate and key (0600), made the first time it's turned on
  ~/.local/state/nimbus/vnc-portal.json  the portal's restore token (not a setting)
  $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/hearth-vnc/         who's connected now (clients.json, watched by the bar) and the control socket

  hearth-vnc status                    JSON: on, running, reach, viewOnly, password set, keyring, input (portal|uinput|
                                       none), addresses, port, fingerprint, who's connected, tips
  hearth-vnc set on|reach|viewOnly V   on on|off (starts or stops hearth-vnc.service), reach tailscale|home, viewOnly on|off
  hearth-vnc password                  the new password on stdin (HEARTH_INPUT); at least 8 characters
  hearth-vnc forget-password           take it out of the keyring (nobody can connect until there's a new one)
  hearth-vnc disconnect ID|all         end that connection (or all of them)
  hearth-vnc session                   Desktop Mode's autostart: starts the service if it's on; never fails
  hearth-vnc serve                     the server (hearth-vnc.service)
Output: one JSON line; failures print "error: ..." and exit 1. No shell anywhere: every command is an argument list.
"""
